"""Vendor digit/icon bitmap tables for the 16x32 (16 rows x 32 cols) device geometry.

Verbatim (only whitespace/newlines normalised) from `ILedClockUtils.java`'s embedded
`*1632` string constants -- these are DECIMAL byte values, one row-byte at a time; see
that file's `dateNumberData1632` etc. Only the `1632` variant is bundled: iLedClock is
always exactly 16 rows x 32 columns, and `getValueByFieldName('style' + i + ...1632')`
is the ONLY variant the app's own DEVICE_ROW==16 && DEVICE_COLUMN==32 branch ever
selects for this hardware (verified from the real control-flow, not inferred).

These are opaque firmware payloads: the DEVICE, not this package, interprets column
widths per style. programs.py sends them verbatim; render.py never decodes them for
preview (the clock-face preview uses our own bundled font instead, flagged `approximate`).
"""

